<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n68238" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μογ-ερός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ός</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Nic.
			<u>Al.</u>
			419
		</span></i> (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				v.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σμυγερός</span>
			): poet. Adj. used by Trag. in anap. and lyr.
				(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόγος</span>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σμογερός</span>): </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> of persons, <i>toiling, distressed,
				wretched</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				565
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Th.</u>
				827
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				783
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				790
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				1207
			</span></i>; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. οἶκοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					93
				</span></i>
			. Adv. -
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ρῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Man.
					1.146
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of things,
				<i>toilsome, grievous</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάματοι</span>
			v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.508
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Emp.
			</span></i> or <i><span class="en">
				Simon.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄχεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					205
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκουαί</span> ear
			<i>trouble</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Marc.Sid.
				86
			</span></i>.</div>
